What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/standby-controller/wakeup_config
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org
Description:
		CV200 DVBIP CVPM ABI 1 wake policy, root read/write only.
		Four base-0 unsigned 32-bit numbers: enabled_mask timeout_seconds
		raw_ir_low raw_ir_high. Bit 0 enables IR; bit 1 enables the C51
		relative timer. Initial policy is "0x2 30 0x00000000 0x00000000"
		unless overridden in DT. Enabled timer requires 1..4294967294
		seconds. Disabled timer requires timeout_seconds=0; at least one
		supported wake source is mandatory. IR words are the selected C51
		raw parser's values, not Linux rc-core scancodes. Configuration is
		frozen throughout suspend and after a failed firmware disarm.
		This is not a generic register-write, OTP, or security control.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/standby-controller/firmware
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org
Description:
		Root-readable CVPM ABI version and advertised wake capabilities.
		Presence proves discovery of the expected resident monitor, not
		that a particular fuse/OEM policy permits C51 takeover or that a
		hardware suspend/resume has succeeded. CONFIG errors are propagated
		when a transition is attempted.
		CONFIG, LAST_WAKE and CANCEL are serialized global operations and
		may be called on any CPU. Linux prepares before offlining secondary
		CPUs and unwinds after re-enabling them. Only the actual ENTER
		operation requires CPU0 with all secondary CPUs offline.
		Deep resume also requires controller context restoration, not just
		a successful firmware return. CV200 pinconf saves/restores its pad
		registers in noirq PM; DW-MMC restores controller interrupts and
		IDMAC before the card can runtime-resume; the monitor preserves
		SC_GEN17's boot-selected GPU SVB corner for the existing OPP policy.
		With no_console_suspend, PL011 must retain/restore its live console
		control register and interrupt mask: TX polling can still print
		with UARTEN lost while interactive RX no longer works.
		ENTER additionally requires a settled core-bus clock selector and
		empty Secure/Non-secure GIC active-priority registers. A late pending
		interrupt rejects entry with -EBUSY; the monitor does not acknowledge
		or discard it. This restricted contract is not a full interrupt-stack
		or secure-payload context switch. Resume verifies the core-bus mux
		acknowledgement and clears the CV200 GEN0 retention marker.
		CV200 USB2 host nodes must use their matching compatible, six CCF
		clocks and four shared reset lines. Their INNO PHY init references
		remain owned across system sleep, with power references still balanced.
		The provider restores MODE and analog state in resume_early, before
		normal host resume accesses controller MMIO. A failed provider restore
		is propagated rather than bypassed. This does not add USB wake support.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/standby-controller/last_wake
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org
Description:
		Root-readable snapshot captured once after a real firmware resume,
		before stopping/cancelling the MCU. Reports source, MCU elapsed
		whole seconds and raw IR words. Before a valid wake, or on an
		invalid/stale firmware record, prints "unavailable error=<errno>".
		A timeout is source 2. Snapshot reads do not consume the cached
		kernel result. No absent cause is converted into a fabricated IR
		or timer wake.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/standby-controller/stats
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org
Description:
		Root-readable attempts, actual firmware resumes, aborted
		transitions, active/armed flags, first transition error, cancellation
		error, wake-record error and sleep-time-injection state. A resume
		count means cpu_resume returned; it does not certify every device,
		DDR byte, clock, audio sample or retained application transaction.
		PM debug tests that return before ENTER increment attempts and
		aborted, not resumes. A successful test must leave active/armed
		clear and last_error/cancel_error zero; it is not a deep-wake pass.
